    [Doc] Document Atlas 850/850E/950 SuperPod PD configuration (#18176)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The multi-node Mooncake PD guide currently covers A2/A3 networking and
    container setup. Add the configuration needed for Atlas 850/850E/950
    SuperPod (Ascend 950PR/950DT) deployments:
    
    - Default super plane (UB port and UBC protocol) with automatic
    `ASCEND_LOCAL_COMM_RES` configuration.
    - UBG and UBoE protocol selection, with hardware support and prior
    network setup required for all parameter-plane options.
    - RoCE endpoint files under `/etc/hixlep`, physical NPU filename
    conventions, and `ascend_local_comm_res_path` placement in the outer
    `MultiConnector` configuration when PD is combined with KV pooling.
    - Required UB/RoCE container devices and mounts, optional `hiroce5`, and
    optional manually generated `route.conf` with a link to the HIXL
    configuration guide.
    
    Keep the existing A2/A3 deployment examples and identify their
    verification scope.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime or API changes. Documentation only.
    
